{"type":"message","id":"9d7b7c41","parentId":"a14f1577","timestamp":"2026-05-17T06:18:15.721Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The server is returning 500 error with \"error code: 1101\". This is likely an error from the Cloudflare Workers backend. The 1101 error in Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker exceeded memory limit\" or a JS error. But the error is coming from the server-side code.\n\nLet me try with a simpler message first to see if it's a content issue.\n\nActually wait - it could be that the POST endpoint expects different field names. Let me check the original POST format by looking at what the history messages look like. Each message has: id, content, threadId, type, timestamp, echoAsset, replyTo. \n\nMaybe the send endpoint needs `message` instead of `content`, or perhaps it requires an `id` field. Let me experiment with different parameter combinations to see what actually works.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2ff4e855-b303-4d3b-a3a3-127de1cc8816","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with 'message' field instead of 'content'\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"message\":\"[Heartbeat 06:15 UTC | 1131分钟节点] test\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":1513,"output":285,"cacheRead":18480,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20278,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778998679321,"responseId":"chatcmpl-78f63828-1bc3-4fe1-a651-2bbd895e6794"}}
